OpenJDK runtime (Eclipse Temurin 21.0.12), Hallym Circuit Studio 2
  A reduced Java runtime made with jlink from Eclipse Temurin 21.0.12, the
  OpenJDK build of the Eclipse Adoptium project (the exact build is what
  runtime/bin/java -version prints, e.g. 21.0.12+1). jlink leaves out the modules the engine
  does not use and strips debug information; the OpenJDK code is not
  changed. It has the modules java.base, java.datatransfer, java.desktop,
  java.logging, java.prefs, java.sql, java.transaction.xa, java.xml,
  jdk.charsets and jdk.unsupported, and a class data archive of the engine
  (hcs-engine.jsa), and runs the engine (hcs-engine.jar) and nothing else.
  Copyright (c) Oracle and/or its affiliates, and the OpenJDK contributors.
  License: GNU General Public License, version 2, with the Classpath
           Exception (and the OpenJDK Assembly Exception); the libraries
           OpenJDK includes carry their own notices.
  Location: runtime/ in the installed program (resources/runtime/, built by
            ./gradlew :engine:runtime). The full license texts are in
            runtime/legal/<module>/: LICENSE, ASSEMBLY_EXCEPTION,
            ADDITIONAL_LICENSE_INFO and a notice for each included library
            (e.g. runtime/legal/java.desktop/freetype.md). About > Licenses
            shows the first three (electron/LICENSE.openjdk.txt).
  Source:  https://adoptium.net/temurin/ (Eclipse Temurin 21; its source at
           https://github.com/adoptium/jdk21u, tag jdk-<that build>, e.g.
           jdk-21.0.12+1) and https://openjdk.org/

